IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Legislation Act 2003 (Commonwealth), sections 12 to 54: every period, date and number of days, months or sittings
-- that the text states, computed in one place.
-- This module imports only prelude and daydate.
-- Text: C2004A01224.txt, compilation C2019C00084; it is not the authorised text.
--
-- Conventions (each is a fork line in NOTES.md):
--   * Dates are written Date day month year.
--   * "N days after E" is the N days that follow the day E: its last day is E plus N, and E itself is not in it.
--     The text uses the same shape in section 46(2) ("the end of 7 days after" a day).
--     A period "within" N days after E includes its last day.
--   * "N months after D" and "the Nth anniversary of D" end on the day with the same day number, N months or years later.
--     Where the target month has no such day the text does not say which day is meant, and the answer is NOTHING (fork F02).
--   * A sitting calendar is an input: the sitting days of one House, in date order.
--     "Within N sitting days of that House after E" counts the sitting days that come after the day E, the first being day 1.
--     A calendar that has fewer than N sitting days after E answers NOTHING.
--   * Where the text does not close a computation the answer is NOTHING and a test asserts it.

§ `Dates and periods of days`

-- src:241 | (1) A legislative instrument or a notifiable instrument commences:
-- src:242 | (a) at the start of the day after the day the instrument is registered; or
-- src:243 | (b) so far as the instrument provides otherwise—in accordance with such provision.
@ref s 12(1) (src:241-243)
GIVEN `the day the instrument is registered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 12(1)(a): the day an instrument commences when it provides nothing else` MEANS
    `the day the instrument is registered` PLUS 1

-- "N days after E": the days that follow the day E.
-- src:512 | (3) The rule-maker must lodge for registration the compilation required by subsection (1) within 28 days after the event occurs, or a longer period allowed by the First Parliamentary Counsel.
@ref s 15R(3) (src:512-512)
GIVEN `the number of days` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of a period of days after an event` MEANS
    `the day of the event` PLUS `the number of days`

GIVEN `the number of days` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the event` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a day falls within a period of days after an event` MEANS
        `the day in question` GREATER THAN `the day of the event`
    AND `the day in question` AT MOST `the last day of a period of days after an event` `the number of days` `the day of the event`

@ref s 15R(3) (src:512-512)
GIVEN `the day the event occurs` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 15R(3): the last day for lodging a compilation after a required compilation event` MEANS
    `the last day of a period of days after an event` 28 `the day the event occurs`

-- src:527 | (2) If a required compilation event occurs for a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, the First Parliamentary Counsel must register a compilation of the instrument:
-- src:528 | (a) if a compilation is lodged for registration within 28 days after the event, or within a longer period allowed by the First Parliamentary Counsel—as soon as practicable after lodgement; or
-- src:529 | (b) if a compilation is not lodged for registration within that period—as soon as practicable after the end of the period.
@ref s 15T(2)(a) (src:527-529)
GIVEN `the day the event occurs` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 15T(2)(a): the last day of the 28 days after a required compilation event` MEANS
    `the last day of a period of days after an event` 28 `the day the event occurs`

-- src:776 | (2) The period referred to in subsection (1) is the period starting on the day on which the original legislative instrument was registered and ending at the end of 7 days after:
-- src:777 | (a) if the original legislative instrument has been laid, in accordance with subsection 38(1), before both Houses of the Parliament on the same day—that day; or
-- src:778 | (b) if the original legislative instrument was so laid before both Houses on different days—the later of those days; or
-- src:779 | (c) if the original legislative instrument has not been so laid before both Houses—the last day on which subsection 38(1) could have been complied with.
@ref s 46(2) (src:776-779)
GIVEN `the day the instrument is laid or the last day it could have been laid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 46(2): the last day of the period in which the same instrument is not to be made` MEANS
    `the last day of a period of days after an event` 7 `the day the instrument is laid or the last day it could have been laid`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE
      `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of two days` MEANS
    IF `the first day` AT LEAST `the second day`
    THEN `the first day`
    ELSE `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE
      `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of two days` MEANS
    IF `the first day` AT MOST `the second day`
    THEN `the first day`
    ELSE `the second day`

@ref s 46(2) (src:776-776)
GIVEN `the day the instrument was registered` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46(2): a day falls in the period starting on the day of registration and ending at the end of its last day` MEANS
        `the day in question` AT LEAST `the day the instrument was registered`
    AND `the day in question` AT MOST `the last day of the period`

§ `Months and years`

-- A target month or year that has no such day: the text does not say, so the answer is NOTHING (fork F02).
-- src:798 | (1) A legislative instrument or a provision of a legislative instrument (the later instrument or provision) that is the same in substance as a legislative instrument or a provision of a legislative instrument (the disallowed instrument or provision) that has been disallowed (or is taken to have been disallowed) under subsection 42(1) or (2) must not be made within 6 months after the day of disallowance.
@ref s 48(1) (src:798-798)
GIVEN `the number of months` IS A NUMBER
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day with the same day number a number of months after a day` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY (`add months` `the day` `the number of months`) EQUALS DATE_DAY `the day`
    THEN JUST (`add months` `the day` `the number of months`)
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the number of years` IS A NUMBER
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the anniversary of a day, a number of years later` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY (`add years` `the day` `the number of years`) EQUALS DATE_DAY `the day`
    THEN JUST (`add years` `the day` `the number of years`)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 48(1) (src:798-798)
GIVEN `the day of disallowance` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 48(1): the last day of the 6 months after the day of disallowance` MEANS
    `the day with the same day number a number of months after a day` 6 `the day of disallowance`

@ref s 48(1) (src:798-798)
GIVEN `the day of disallowance` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(1): a day falls within the 6 months after the day of disallowance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 48(1): the last day of the 6 months after the day of disallowance` `the day of disallowance`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `the last day` THEN JUST (`the day in question` GREATER THAN `the day of disallowance` AND `the day in question` AT MOST `the last day`)

§ `Sitting days`

GIVEN `the sitting days of the House, in date order` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the sitting days after a day` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN x YIELD x GREATER THAN `the day`) `the sitting days of the House, in date order`

GIVEN `the number n` IS A NUMBER
      `the sitting days of the House, in date order` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the nth sitting day after a day` MEANS
    IF (`the number n` AT LEAST 1) AND (`the number n` AT MOST count `the later sitting days`)
    THEN JUST (at `the later sitting days` (`the number n` MINUS 1))
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the later sitting days` MEANS `the sitting days after a day` `the sitting days of the House, in date order` `the day`

GIVEN `the sitting days of the House, in date order` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the first sitting day after a day` MEANS
    `the nth sitting day after a day` 1 `the sitting days of the House, in date order` `the day`

-- "within N sitting days of that House ... beginning on the first sitting day after" the day:
-- the window runs from the first sitting day after the day to the Nth.
GIVEN `the number n` IS A NUMBER
      `the sitting days of the House, in date order` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a day falls within the first n sitting days after a day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the first sitting day after a day` `the sitting days of the House, in date order` `the day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `the first one` THEN
        CONSIDER `the nth sitting day after a day` `the number n` `the sitting days of the House, in date order` `the day`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST `the last one` THEN JUST (`the day in question` AT LEAST `the first one` AND `the day in question` AT MOST `the last one`)

-- The numbers of sitting days the text fixes, each stated once and used by the functions below.
-- A "sitting day count" is the position of a sitting day of the House after an event: the first sitting day after the event is 1.
-- src:721 | (1) The Office of Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for a copy of each registered legislative instrument to be delivered to each House of the Parliament to be laid before each House within 6 sitting days of that House after the registration of the instrument.
@ref s 38(1) (src:721-721)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(1): the number of sitting days allowed for laying` MEANS 6

GIVEN `the sitting day count on which the instrument is laid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38(1): a sitting day count is within the time for laying` MEANS
    `the sitting day count on which the instrument is laid` AT LEAST 1 AND `the sitting day count on which the instrument is laid` AT MOST `s 38(1): the number of sitting days allowed for laying`

-- src:347 | (2) The First Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for a copy of the correct version of the instrument to be delivered to each House of the Parliament to be laid before each House within 6 sitting days of that House after the rectification.
@ref s 15DA(2) (src:347-347)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 15DA(2): the number of sitting days allowed for laying` MEANS 6

-- src:742 | (1) If:
-- src:743 | (a) notice of a motion to disallow a legislative instrument or a provision of a legislative instrument is given in a House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after a copy of the instrument was laid before that House; and
-- src:744 | (b) within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after the giving of that notice, the House passes a resolution, in pursuance of the motion, disallowing the instrument or provision;
-- src:745 | the instrument or provision so disallowed is repealed immediately after the passing of that resolution.
@ref s 42(1) (src:742-745)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 42(1): the number of sitting days allowed` MEANS 15

GIVEN `the sitting day count on which the step is taken` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 42(1): a sitting day count is within the time allowed` MEANS
    `the sitting day count on which the step is taken` AT LEAST 1 AND `the sitting day count on which the step is taken` AT MOST `s 42(1): the number of sitting days allowed`

-- src:721 | (1) The Office of Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for a copy of each registered legislative instrument to be delivered to each House of the Parliament to be laid before each House within 6 sitting days of that House after the registration of the instrument.
@ref s 38(1) (src:721-721)
GIVEN `the sitting days of the House, in date order` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day the instrument was registered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 38(1): the last day for laying a registered legislative instrument before a House` MEANS
    `the nth sitting day after a day` `s 38(1): the number of sitting days allowed for laying` `the sitting days of the House, in date order` `the day the instrument was registered`

-- src:347 | (2) The First Parliamentary Counsel must arrange for a copy of the correct version of the instrument to be delivered to each House of the Parliament to be laid before each House within 6 sitting days of that House after the rectification.
@ref s 15DA(2) (src:347-347)
GIVEN `the sitting days of the House, in date order` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day of the rectification` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 15DA(2): the last day for laying the correct version before a House` MEANS
    `the nth sitting day after a day` `s 15DA(2): the number of sitting days allowed for laying` `the sitting days of the House, in date order` `the day of the rectification`

-- src:359 | at the time the correct version of the instrument is laid before a House as mentioned in subsection (2)—that notice of motion is taken to have been given in that House on the sitting day of that House after the correct version of the instrument is laid before that House;
@ref s 15DA(3)(e) (src:359-359)
GIVEN `the sitting days of the House, in date order` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day the correct version is laid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 15DA(3)(e): the sitting day after the correct version is laid` MEANS
    `the first sitting day after a day` `the sitting days of the House, in date order` `the day the correct version is laid`

-- src:742 | (1) If:
-- src:743 | (a) notice of a motion to disallow a legislative instrument or a provision of a legislative instrument is given in a House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after a copy of the instrument was laid before that House; and
-- src:744 | (b) within 15 sitting days of that House beginning on the first sitting day after the giving of that notice, the House passes a resolution, in pursuance of the motion, disallowing the instrument or provision;
