`s 42(1)(b): the resolution is passed in time` MEANS
    `a day falls within the first n sitting days after a day` `s 42(1): the number of sitting days allowed` `the sitting days of the House, in date order` `the day notice was given` `the day the resolution was passed`

-- The last day on which an instrument may be disallowed in a House (section 48A(2)(aa)): notice on the last day allowed,
-- then the resolution on the last day allowed after that notice.
@ref s 42(1) (src:742-745)
GIVEN `the sitting days of the House, in date order` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day the instrument was laid before the House` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day on which a legislative instrument may be disallowed in a House` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 42(1)(a): the last day on which notice of a motion to disallow may be given` `the sitting days of the House, in date order` `the day the instrument was laid before the House`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `the last day for notice` THEN `s 42(1)(b): the last day on which the House may pass the resolution after notice` `the sitting days of the House, in date order` `the last day for notice`

§ `Sunsetting`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a day is a 1 April or a 1 October` MEANS
        DATE_DAY `the day` EQUALS 1
    AND (   DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 4
         OR DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 10)

-- src:889 | (1) This subsection repeals a legislative instrument on the first 1 April or 1 October falling on or after the tenth anniversary of registration of the instrument, unless the instrument was registered on 1 January 2005.
@ref s 50(1) (src:889-889)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first 1 April or 1 October on or after a day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day` AT MOST (Date 1 4 (DATE_YEAR `the day`)) THEN Date 1 4 (DATE_YEAR `the day`)
           IF `the day` AT MOST (Date 1 10 (DATE_YEAR `the day`)) THEN Date 1 10 (DATE_YEAR `the day`)
           OTHERWISE Date 1 4 (DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS 1)

@ref s 50(1) (src:889-889)
GIVEN `the day the instrument was registered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 50(1): this subsection applies to an instrument registered on` MEANS
    NOT (`the day the instrument was registered` EQUALS Date 1 1 2005)

-- The function answers with the day only when the same-day-number rule read back and read forward gives one answer (fork F02).
@ref s 50(1) (src:889-889)
GIVEN `the day the instrument was registered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 50(1): the day a legislative instrument is repealed by sunsetting` MEANS
    IF NOT `s 50(1): this subsection applies to an instrument registered on` `the day the instrument was registered`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the first 1 April or 1 October on or after the 10th anniversary, read back` EQUALS `the first 1 April or 1 October on or after the 10th anniversary, read forward`
         THEN JUST `the first 1 April or 1 October on or after the 10th anniversary, read back`
         ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the first 1 April or 1 October on or after the 10th anniversary, read back` MEANS
            `the first 1 April or 1 October on or after a day` (`add years` `the day the instrument was registered` 10)
        `the first 1 April or 1 October on or after the 10th anniversary, read forward` MEANS
            `the first 1 April or 1 October on or after a day` (Date (DATE_DAY `the day the instrument was registered`) (DATE_MONTH `the day the instrument was registered`) (DATE_YEAR `the day the instrument was registered` PLUS 10))

-- src:890 | (2) This subsection repeals a legislative instrument on the day worked out using the table if the instrument was registered on 1 January 2005.
-- src:891 | Day of repeal of legislative instrument registered on 1 January 2005
-- src:892 | Year the instrument was made
-- src:893 | Day of repeal
-- src:894 | 1
-- src:895 | A year before 1930
-- src:896 | 1 April 2015
-- src:897 | 2
-- src:898 | A year in the decade starting on 1 January 1930
-- src:899 | 1 October 2015
-- src:900 | 3
-- src:901 | A year in the decade starting on 1 January 1940
-- src:902 | 1 April 2016
-- src:903 | 4
-- src:904 | A year in the decade starting on 1 January 1950
-- src:905 | 1 October 2016
-- src:906 | 5
-- src:907 | A year in the decade starting on 1 January 1960
-- src:908 | 1 April 2017
-- src:909 | 6
-- src:910 | A year in the decade starting on 1 January 1970
-- src:911 | 1 October 2017
-- src:912 | 7
-- src:913 | A year in the decade starting on 1 January 1980
-- src:914 | 1 April 2018
-- src:915 | 8
-- src:916 | 1990, 1991, 1992, 1993 or 1994
-- src:917 | 1 October 2018
-- src:918 | 9
-- src:919 | 1995, 1996, 1997, 1998 or 1999
-- src:920 | 1 April 2019
-- src:921 | 10
-- src:922 | 2000, 2001 or 2002
-- src:923 | 1 October 2019
-- src:924 | 11
-- src:925 | 2003 or 2004
-- src:926 | 1 April 2020
@ref s 50(2) (src:890-926)
GIVEN `the year the instrument was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 50(2): the day an instrument registered on 1 January 2005 is repealed, by the year it was made` MEANS
    --                                                                                                                      day of repeal
    BRANCH IF `the year the instrument was made` LESS THAN 1930                                                         THEN JUST (Date 1 4 2015)
           IF (`the year the instrument was made` AT LEAST 1930) AND (`the year the instrument was made` AT MOST 1939) THEN JUST (Date 1 10 2015)
           IF (`the year the instrument was made` AT LEAST 1940) AND (`the year the instrument was made` AT MOST 1949) THEN JUST (Date 1 4 2016)
           IF (`the year the instrument was made` AT LEAST 1950) AND (`the year the instrument was made` AT MOST 1959) THEN JUST (Date 1 10 2016)
           IF (`the year the instrument was made` AT LEAST 1960) AND (`the year the instrument was made` AT MOST 1969) THEN JUST (Date 1 4 2017)
           IF (`the year the instrument was made` AT LEAST 1970) AND (`the year the instrument was made` AT MOST 1979) THEN JUST (Date 1 10 2017)
           IF (`the year the instrument was made` AT LEAST 1980) AND (`the year the instrument was made` AT MOST 1989) THEN JUST (Date 1 4 2018)
           IF (   `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 1990 OR `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 1991
               OR `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 1992 OR `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 1993
               OR `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 1994)                                                       THEN JUST (Date 1 10 2018)
           IF (   `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 1995 OR `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 1996
               OR `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 1997 OR `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 1998
               OR `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 1999)                                                       THEN JUST (Date 1 4 2019)
           IF (   `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 2000 OR `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 2001
               OR `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 2002)                                                       THEN JUST (Date 1 10 2019)
           IF (   `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 2003 OR `the year the instrument was made` EQUALS 2004)    THEN JUST (Date 1 4 2020)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 50(2) (src:890-890)
GIVEN `the day the instrument was registered` IS A DATE
      `the year the instrument was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ss 50(1) and (2): the day a legislative instrument is repealed by sunsetting, by registration day and year made` MEANS
    IF `the day the instrument was registered` EQUALS Date 1 1 2005
    THEN `s 50(2): the day an instrument registered on 1 January 2005 is repealed, by the year it was made` `the year the instrument was made`
    ELSE `s 50(1): the day a legislative instrument is repealed by sunsetting` `the day the instrument was registered`

-- src:931 | (1) If:
-- src:932 | (a) a legislative instrument would (apart from this section) be repealed by section 50 or 51A on a particular day (the sunsetting day); and
-- src:933 | (b) the Attorney-General is satisfied, on written application by the rule-maker:
-- src:934 | (i) that the instrument would (apart from the operation of this Part) be likely to cease to be in force within 24 months after the sunsetting day; or
-- src:935 | (ii) that an instrument proposed to be made in substitution for the instrument will not be able to be completed before the sunsetting day for reasons that the rule-maker could not have foreseen and avoided or because the dissolution or expiration of the House of Representatives or the prorogation of the Parliament renders it inappropriate to make a replacement instrument before a new government is formed; or
-- src:936 | (iii) that the Attorney-General has approved this Part not applying to the instrument;
-- src:937 | then:
-- src:938 | (c) the Attorney-General may issue a certificate providing that the first-mentioned instrument is repealed by this section on a 1 April or 1 October that is on or before the second anniversary of the sunsetting day and that is specified in the certificate; and
-- src:939 | (d) if the Attorney-General issues the certificate, the first-mentioned instrument is repealed by this section on the specified day instead of the sunsetting day, unless the instrument has been repealed earlier.
@ref s 51(1)(b) to (d) (src:931-939)
GIVEN `the sunsetting day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 51(1)(b)(i): the last day of the 24 months after the sunsetting day` MEANS
    `the day with the same day number a number of months after a day` 24 `the sunsetting day`

@ref s 51(1)(c) (src:938-938)
GIVEN `the sunsetting day` IS A DATE
      `the day specified in the certificate` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(1)(c): the day specified is a 1 April or 1 October on or before the second anniversary of the sunsetting day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the anniversary of a day, a number of years later` 2 `the sunsetting day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `the second anniversary` THEN JUST (`a day is a 1 April or a 1 October` `the day specified in the certificate` AND `the day specified in the certificate` AT MOST `the second anniversary`)

-- src:941 | (4) Section 42 does not apply to a certificate issued under paragraph (1)(c) if the day specified in the certificate is on or before the first anniversary of the sunsetting day.
@ref s 51(4) (src:941-941)
GIVEN `the sunsetting day` IS A DATE
      `the day specified in the certificate` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(4): the day specified is on or before the first anniversary of the sunsetting day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the anniversary of a day, a number of years later` 1 `the sunsetting day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `the first anniversary` THEN JUST (`the day specified in the certificate` AT MOST `the first anniversary`)

-- src:949 | (2) The day specified in the sunset-altering instrument:
-- src:950 | (a) must be 1 April or 1 October of a year; and
-- src:951 | (b) must be not more than 5 years after the earliest day on which any of the instruments to be reviewed would be repealed by section 50 or 51 apart from this section; and
-- src:952 | (c) may be the same as, or different from, any of the days on which any of the instruments to be reviewed would be repealed by section 50 or 51 apart from this section.
@ref s 51A(2) (src:949-952)
GIVEN `the earliest day on which any of the instruments would be repealed` IS A DATE
      `the day specified in the sunset-altering instrument` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51A(2): the day specified is a 1 April or 1 October not more than 5 years after the earliest day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the anniversary of a day, a number of years later` 5 `the earliest day on which any of the instruments would be repealed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `the fifth anniversary` THEN JUST (`a day is a 1 April or a 1 October` `the day specified in the sunset-altering instrument` AND `the day specified in the sunset-altering instrument` AT MOST `the fifth anniversary`)

-- A sunsetting day, in the sense of section 52(1), is the first possible day of repeal under Part 4 of Chapter 3
-- and each 1 April and 1 October after that day.
-- src:956 | (1) In this section:
-- src:957 | list tabling day, in relation to a sunsetting day and to a House of the Parliament, means the first sitting day of that House occurring within 18 months before that sunsetting day.
-- src:958 | sunsetting day means the first possible day on which any legislative instrument will be repealed by this Part and each 1 April and 1 October occurring after that day.
@ref s 52(1) (src:956-958)
GIVEN `the first possible day of repeal` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52(1): a day is a sunsetting day` MEANS
        `the day` EQUALS `the first possible day of repeal`
    OR (    `the day` GREATER THAN `the first possible day of repeal`
        AND `a day is a 1 April or a 1 October` `the day`)

@ref s 52(1) (src:957-957)
GIVEN `the sitting days of the House, in date order` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the sunsetting day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 52(1): the list tabling day for a House and a sunsetting day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day with the same day number a number of months after a day` (0 MINUS 18) `the sunsetting day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `the first day of the 18 months` THEN
        IF null `the sitting days in the 18 months`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (at `the sitting days in the 18 months` 0)
        WHERE
            `the sitting days in the 18 months` MEANS
                filter (GIVEN x YIELD (x AT LEAST `the first day of the 18 months`) AND (x LESS THAN `the sunsetting day`)) `the sitting days of the House, in date order`

-- src:968 | (2) The legislative instrument continues in force, subject to:
-- src:969 | (a) sections 50, 51 and 51A, which apply to it after the passage of the resolution as if it were registered on the day on which it would have been repealed by section 50, 51 or 51A apart from this section; and
-- src:970 | (b) any later instrument amending or repealing it.
@ref s 53(2)(a) (src:968-970)
GIVEN `the repeal day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 53(2)(a): the next sunsetting day of an instrument continued by resolution` MEANS
    `s 50(1): the day a legislative instrument is repealed by sunsetting` `the repeal day`

§ `Events in time (sections 48A to 48D)`

DECLARE `Event in time` HAS
    `the day the event occurs`                IS A DATE
    `the event occurs at the end of the day` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day count of a date` MEANS Day `the date`

GIVEN `the event` IS AN `Event in time`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the instant of an event, counted in half days` MEANS
    (`the day count of a date` (`the event`'s `the day the event occurs`) TIMES 2)
    PLUS (IF `the event`'s `the event occurs at the end of the day` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

-- Sections 48A(2) and 48B(2): "the day after the latest" (or "the later") of the events.
-- src:813 | (2) The repeal of the instrument by this section happens on the day after the latest of the following events occurs, unless the instrument has been repealed earlier by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2):
-- src:814 | (aa) for a disallowable legislative instrument—the end of the last day on which the instrument or a provision of the instrument may be disallowed in a House of the Parliament;
-- src:815 | (a) for any legislative instrument or notifiable instrument—whichever of the following is applicable:
-- src:816 | (i) the commencement of the instrument, or of the last of its provisions to commence;
-- src:817 | (ii) if the last of its provisions that have not commenced are repealed, or cannot commence because of the occurrence of an event—that repeal, or the occurrence of that event;
-- src:818 | (b) for a legislative instrument to which section 42 does not apply or for a notifiable instrument—the registration of the instrument.
@ref s 48A(2) (src:813-818)
GIVEN `the days on which the events occur` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day after the latest of the days on which events occur` MEANS
    IF null `the days on which the events occur`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (Date ((maximum (map `the day count of a date` `the days on which the events occur`)) PLUS 1))

-- Section 48A(2): the events that apply depend on the instrument: paragraph (aa) for a disallowable legislative instrument,
-- paragraph (a) for every instrument, paragraph (b) for a legislative instrument to which section 42 does not apply or a notifiable instrument.
@ref s 48A(2) (src:813-818)
GIVEN `the instrument is a disallowable legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day on which the instrument or a provision of it may be disallowed in a House` IS A DATE
      `the day the instrument commences, or the last of its provisions to commence` IS A DATE
      `the day the instrument is registered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 48A(2): the day on which the repeal by this section happens` MEANS
    `the day after the latest of the days on which events occur`
        (IF `the instrument is a disallowable legislative instrument`
         THEN LIST `the last day on which the instrument or a provision of it may be disallowed in a House`, `the day the instrument commences, or the last of its provisions to commence`
         ELSE LIST `the day the instrument commences, or the last of its provisions to commence`, `the day the instrument is registered`)

-- Sections 48C(2) and 48D(2): "immediately after the latest" of the events.
-- An event at the end of a day (the end of the last day on which disallowance may happen) is followed by the next day;
-- an event at the start of a day (a commencement) is followed by that same day.
-- src:844 | (2) The repeal of the provision by this section happens immediately after the latest of the following events occurs, unless the provision has been repealed earlier by subsection 38(3) or 42(1) or (2):
-- src:845 | (aa) if the provision is in a disallowable legislative instrument—the end of the last day on which the instrument or a provision of the instrument may be disallowed in a House of the Parliament;
-- src:846 | (a) if the provision is in any legislative instrument or notifiable instrument—whichever of the following is applicable:
-- src:847 | (i) the commencement of the provision;
-- src:848 | (ii) if the provision cannot commence because of the occurrence of an event—the occurrence of that event;
-- src:849 | (b) if the provision is in a legislative instrument to which section 42 does not apply or is in a notifiable instrument—the registration of the legislative instrument or notifiable instrument.
@ref s 48C(2) (src:844-849)
GIVEN `the events` IS A LIST OF `Event in time`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day on which a repeal immediately after the latest event happens` MEANS
    IF null `the events`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (Date (FLOOR (((maximum (map `the instant of an event, counted in half days` `the events`)) PLUS 1) DIVIDED BY 2)))
